 ## Not yet confirmed

-The font on tooltips. The document square body font. Where the vitals bars are drawn. The inside of `render_bay`, `render_bar_slot` and `under_the_tree` (judged from usage counts only). Whether `hacker.toml`'s `curvature` key is read (it is not in `FileEffects`).
+Native tooltip family inheritance remains unverified. Document bodies dispatch through their backends; do not treat the body as inherited management text. Vitals are drawn by the wall's `bar_row` closure (main.rs:29765). Bay/slot and the non-painting drag helper are classified above. The legacy hacker.toml `curvature` key has no FileEffects field; author against Grade::warp instead.
+
+## Using this as an authoring checklist
+
+Record material, boundary, emphasis and type separately. The route column is a source-map summary, not a native coverage receipt. Expand workbench Kind templates, composer and menus before certifying that family. The corner guard checks corners only.
+
+Custom TOML can select compiled strategies. It cannot yet author grain, lift, marker geometry or optical font policy: these remain renderer code, and Paper applies the Caveat correction independently of the selected UI family. Keep this capability boundary visible in an authoring skill.
